# Spoken nouns (locked decision — apply Monday in one pass)

- **booking** — primary noun in all spoken / visible UI (vendor and client).
- **/projects** — keep in URLs and code identifiers (`/vendor/projects`, `projectId`, etc.). Do not rename routes in the Monday copy pass unless explicitly asked.
- **job** — only as a *type* label if needed (prefer “booking type”). Never “open any job”, “add the job”, etc.
- **event** — only when the booking genuinely is an event. Prefer booking / session / appointment for other services.

Do not mix Projects / booking / job in the same vendor sentence. Client-facing share text and portal headers must not say “project” or overclaim “secure”.

Related parked work: Money tab simplification canvas + voice audit — revisit with tester evidence; do not preempt with broad rewrites.
